1. Title Page
Project Title: Binance Futures Trading Bot (Testnet)

Author: Dhairya Mittal

Date: January 27, 2026

Objective: To develop a modular Python application for automated trading on the Binance Futures Testnet.

2. System Architecture
Describe the modular design you implemented (as seen in your src structure):

client.py: Handles API authentication and session management.

orders.py: Encapsulates the logic for Market and Limit order creation.

validators.py: Ensures all user inputs (symbol, quantity, price) meet exchange requirements before execution.

logging_config.py: Manages detailed logging of every API request and response to bot.log.

3. Bug Fixes & Technical Challenges
Explain how you resolved critical errors encountered during development:

Timestamp Sync (Error -1021):

Problem: Local system clock drift caused requests to be rejected.

Solution: Implemented a synchronization step that calculates the timestamp_offset between the local machine and the Binance server before placing orders.

Price Filter (Error -4024):

Problem: Limit sell orders were rejected for being too far below the current mark price.

Solution: Updated validation logic to ensure limit prices comply with exchange PERCENT_PRICE filters.

4. Implementation Results (Screenshots)
Include screenshots of your terminal showing the successful execution of your orders.

Market Order: Status FILLED, showing the avgPrice.

Limit Order: Status NEW, showing the order placed in the order book.

5. Conclusion
A brief summary stating that the bot successfully meets all core requirements, including secure credential management via .env and comprehensive error handling.